$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the Catalytic
Asymmetric Vinylogous Mukaiyama Aldol Addition: Preparation of
(E)-(S)-5-furan-2-yl-5-hydroxy-2-methylpent- 2-enethioic acid
S-tert-butyl ester SI18. The crude reaction mixture was obtained by
following the general procedure for the catalytic asymmetric vinylogous
Mukaiyama aldol addition using furaldehyde (62.0 μL, 0.745 mmol, 1.00 eq)
as starting material and was purified by flash chromatography using a 2.5
× 18 cm silica gel column eluting with a solvent mixture of 5%
acetone/hexanes (1200 mL). The eluant was collected in 30 mL portions and
the product containing fractions (14 to 30) were combined and
concentrated to give alcohol SI18 (201 mg, 0.749 mmol, quant.) as a clear
colorless oil. The ratio of enantiomers was determined to be er = 91:9 by
1H NMR analysis of the mixture of the corresponding diasteromeric
(R)-MTPA esters by comparison of the integrals for the triplets at 6.61
ppm and 6.52 ppm for the major and minor diastereomers, respectively, and
by comparing of the integrals for the singlets at 3.53 ppm and 3.45 ppm
for the major and minor diastereomers, respectively Rf 0.38 (25%
EtOAc/hexanes); Rf 0.36 (20% acetone/hexanes); [α]D 20 -5.5 (c = 1.065,
CHCl3); 500 MHz 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.40 – 7.39 (m, 1H), 6.70 (ddq, J = 7.3,
7.3, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 6.35 (dd, J = 3.4, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 6.27 (d, J = 3.4 Hz,
1H), 4.84 (dd, J = 6.9, 6.4 Hz, 1H), 2.74 (m, 2H), 2.13 (bs, 1H), 1.85
(s, 3H),1.49 (s, 9H); 125 MHz 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 195.0, 155.8, 142.5,
139.4, 134.2, 110.5, 106.6, 67.0, 47.7, 35.1, 30.1 (3), 12.8; 125 MHz
DEPT (CDCl3) δ CH3: 30.1 (3), 12.8. CH2: 35.1. CH: 142.5, 134.2, 110.6,
106.6, 67.0. C: 195.0, 155.8, 139.4, 47.7; IR (neat) 3426, 2995, 2963,
2919, 2863, 1650, 1505, 1479, 1456, 1389, 1364, 1333, 1309, 1266, 1231,
1162, 1051, 1011, 949, 893 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C14H20O3S: C, 62.66; H,
7.51. Found: C, 62.90; H, 7.49.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 4A mol. sieves used
