$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method B; To a solution of 4,6-dibromoisatin (562 mg, 1.84 mmol) in dry
dichloromethane (50 mL) under argon atmosphere was carefully dropped
titanium tetrachloride (0.60 mL, 1.0 M in dichloromethane) at -78 °C.
After stirring for 30 min at 0 °C, the solution of vinylketene N,O-acetal
(100 mg, 0.31 mmol) in dry dichloromethane (10 mL) was added dropwise at
-78 °C. After stirring for 6 hr, to the reaction mixture was added
pyridine (0.20 mL). The resulting mixture was poured to the mixture of a
saturated aqueous solution of (+/-)-sodium potassium tartrate and a
saturated aqueous solution of sodium bicarbonate (1 : 1) at 0 °C. After
the organic layer was clear, aqueous layer was extracted with
dichloromethane. The combined extracts were washed with brine, dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified via column chromatography (Hexane /Chloroform /
Ethyl acetate = 3 / 1 / 1) to afford alcohol, yield 158 mg, 100% as a 70
: 1 diastereomeric mixture. TLC, Rf = 0.17 (Hexane / Ethyl acetate = 1 /
1); m.p. 74~80 °C; IR (neat) 3281, 2964, 1782, 1736, 1685, 1607, 1575
cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz) δ 0.88 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.92 (d, J = 7.1 Hz,
3H), 2.01 (s, 3H), 2.34 (d sept, J = 4.2, 7.1 Hz, 1H), 2.70 (dd, J = 5.8,
13.9 Hz, 1H), 3.38 (dd, J = 9.8, 13.9 Hz, 1H), 4.20 (br, 1H), 4.21 (dd, J
= 5.1, 9.0 Hz, 1H), 4.34 (dd, J = 8.8, 9.0 Hz, 1H), 4.51 (ddd, J = 4.2,
5.1, 8.8 Hz, 1H), 5.92 (dd, J = 5.8, 9.8 Hz, 1H), 6.96 (d, J = 1.2 Hz,
1H), 7.36 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.18 (br, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz) δ 13.9,
14.8, 17.8, 28.3, 33.8, 58.0, 63.6, 77.2, 113.0, 119.9, 123.8, 127.1,
127.5, 129.3, 136.4, 143.3, 153.9, 171.4, 178.3; [α]D -87.3 (c 1.00,
MeOH); HRMS (EI) calcd for C19H20Br2N2O5 (M+) 513.9739, 515.9719,
517.9698, found 513.9730, 515.9750.
