$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 10. A procedure for Mukaiyama aldol reaction in the presence of 3a-OH, L
and PhOTMS (Eq. 7): Freshly distilled THF (2 mL) was injected at room
temperature under nitrogen into pyrexSchrenk tube containing 3a-OH (28.4
mg, 0.10 mmol) and L (95.6 mg, 0.20 mmol). To this solution,
hexamethyldisilazane sodium salt (1.9 M in THF, 0.10 mmol) was added at
room tempearure. The brown mixture was stirred for 10 min at that
temperature, and then cooled to –78 °C and stirred for 5 min at that
temperature. Benzophenone (182 mg, 1.0 mmol), TMS enolate 4a (209 mg, 1.2
mmol), and then trimethylphenoxysilane (16.6 mg, 0.10 mmol) were added.
The brown mixture was stirred at –78 °C for 2 h by monitoring with TLC,
and the reaction mixture was diluted with sat. NaHCO3 aqueous solution
(10 mL). The mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate (15 mL × 2), and
the combined organic layer was washed by brine (10 mL), dried over MgSO4
and evaporated under reduced pressure to give the aldol product which was
purified by flash neutral silica gel column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt
= 10/1) (391 mg, >109% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
