$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8. A procedure for 5b·L2-catalyzed Mukaiyama aldol reaction: Freshly
distilled THF (100mL) was injected at room temperature under nitrogen
into pyrex Schrenk tube containing sodium phenoxide (5b) (58.0 mg, 0.5
mmol) and 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphoryl)benzene (L) (478 mg, 1.0 mmol). The
mixture was stirred for 15 min at that temperature, and then this
colorless solution was cooled to –78 °C and stirred for 5 min at that
temperature. Benzophenone (1a) (18.2 g, 100 mmol), and then TMS enolate
(4a) (20.9 g, 120 mmol) were added. The pale yellow solution was stirred
at –78 °C for 6 h by monitoring with TLC, and the reaction mixture was
diluted with sat. NaHCO3 aqueous solution (100 mL). The mixture was
extracted with ethyl acetate (50 mL × 3), and the combined organic layer
was washed by brine (100 mL), dried over MgSO4 and evaporated under
reduced pressure to give the aldol product which was purified by flash
neutral silica gel column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt = 50/1–1/1) (34.8
g, 97.8% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, Mukaiyama aldol reaction, optimization
study (optimized on catalysts)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Sodium Phenoxide-Phosphine Oxides as Extremely Active Lewis Base
Catalysts for the Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction with Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hatano, Manabu; Takagi, Eri; Ishihara, Kazuaki
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(22), 4527-4530

