$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of aldehyde (0.8 mmol) in
propionitrile (0.32 mL) was added over 10 min to a mixed solution of the
silyl enol ether (0.96 mmol) and 2d (0.08 mmol) in propionitrile (0.65
mL). 3-Hydroxy-2-methyl-1-phenyl-1-hexanone (Table 3), yield 99%. 1H NMR,
13C NMR, and IR spectroscopic data are in agreement with those reported
in the literature. The syn/anti ratio was determined by 1H NMR
spectroscopy: 1H NMR (CDCl3 , 300 MHz) δ 3.79-3.91 (m, 1H, CHOH (anti
isomer)) 4.02-4.08 (m, 1H, CHOH (syn isomer)); The enantiomeric ratios
were determined by HPLC analysis (Daicel OD-H column with
hexane-i-PrOH=9:1, flow rate=1.0 mL/min): t R=6.0 (syn, minor
enantiomer), 6.5 (syn, major enantiomer & anti, one enantiomer), 7.4
(anti, another enantiomer) min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative prepn. gave lower yields and selectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Scope and Limitations of Chiral
B-[3,5-Bis(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]oxazaborolidine Catalyst for Use in the
Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ishihara, Kazuaki; Kondo, Shoichi; Yamamoto, Hisashi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2000), 65(26), 9125-9128

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME68 STEP1
