$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of aldehyde (0.8 mmol) in
propionitrile (0.32 mL) was added over 10 min to a mixed solution of the
silyl enol ether (0.96 mmol) and 2d (0.08 mmol) in propionitrile (0.65
mL). 2,4-Dimethyl-3-hydroxy-1-phenyl-1-pentanone (Table 3): yield 99%. 1H
NMR, 13C NMR, and IR spectroscopic data are in agreement with those
reported in the literature.6 The syn/anti ratio was determined by 1H NMR
spectroscopy: 1H NMR (CDCl3 , 300 MHz) δ 2.94 (d, J=7.5 Hz, 1H, OH (anti
isomer)), 3.12 (d, J=2.7 Hz, 1H, OH (syn isomer)); The enantiomeric
ratios were determined by HPLC analysis (two linear Daicel OD-H columns
with hexane-i-PrOH=80:1, flow rate=0.6 mL/min): tR=28.8 (syn, major
enantiomer), 33.3 (anti, one enantiomer), 35.5 (syn, minor enantiomer),
47.1 (anti, another enantiomer) min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
