$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7. A general procedure for 4b·L2-catalyzed Mukaiyama aldol reaction with
ketones: Freshly distilled THF (5 mL) was injected at room temperature
under nitrogen into pyrex Schrenk tube containing sodium phenoxide (5b)
(2.9 mg, 0.025 mmol) and 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphoryl)benzene (L) (23.9 mg,
0.050 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10 min at that temperature, and
then this colorless solution was cooled to –78 °C and stirred for 5 min
at that temperature.
3-(diphenyl(trimethylsilyloxy)methyl)-dihydrofuran-2(3H)-one (3f). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ – 0.12 (s, 9H), 2.25-2.35 (m, 2H), 3.23 (dt, J = 8.4,
7.8 Hz, 1H), 3.83 (dd, J = 8.7, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 3.97 (ddd, J = 8.7, 7.8, 6.0
Hz, 1H), 7.26-7.45 (m, 10H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.7, 25.7, 48.1,
65.9, 81.9, 127.7, 127.8, 127.9, 128.2, 128.5, 143.7, 144.2, 175.6.
IR(KBr) 3052, 2955, 1756, 1446, 1381, 1251, 1154, 1061 cm-1. HRMS(FAB+)
calcd for C20H24NaO3Si [M+Na]+ 363.1392, found 363.1399.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
