$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7. A general procedure for 4b·L2-catalyzed Mukaiyama aldol reaction with
ketones: Freshly distilled THF (5 mL) was injected at room temperature
under nitrogen into pyrex Schrenk tube containing sodium phenoxide (5b)
(2.9 mg, 0.025 mmol) and 1,2-bis(diphenylphosphoryl)benzene (L) (23.9 mg,
0.050 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10 min at that temperature, and
then this colorless solution was cooled to –78 °C and stirred for 5 min
at that temperature. ethyl
2,2-dimethyl-3,3-diphenyl-3-(trimethylsilyloxy)propanoate (3b). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ – 0.15 (s, 9H), 1.22 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.26 (s,
6H), 4.12 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.19-7.28 (m, 6H), 7.31-7.41 (m, 4H). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.9, 14.1, 24.5, 50.7, 60.5, 85.9, 126.8, 127.0,
129.8, 145.5, 177.4. IR(film) 2977, 2955, 1730, 1715, 1445, 1249, 1143,
1108, 1077, 1029 cm-1. HRMS(FAB+) calcd for C22H30NaO3Si [M+Na]+
393.1862, found 393.1866.
