$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure of Mukaiyama aldol reaction
Aldehyde (2, 2 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (8 mL), and the solution was
cooled to -30 °C. Then TiCl4 (2 mL, 1.0 M in CH2Cl2) was added slowly
under N2 atmosphere. After 15 min, a solution of silyl enol ether (1, 2
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) was added to the mixture dropwise and the mixture
was allowed to react under -30 °C for 1.5 h. After hydrolysis with 5 %
K2CO3 at -30 °C and warm-up, the organic layer was separated and the
aqueous layer was extracted with ether (8 mL× 3). The combined organic
layers were washed with saturated NaCl aqueous (20 mL× 3) and dried over
with Na2SO4. After concentration, product 3 was isolated by flash column
chromatography on silica gel using hexane/Et2O mixture as eluent.
2-fluoro-3-hydroxy-2,4,4-trimethyl-1-phenylpentan-1-one (3h) anti isomer:
white solid; Yield 98%, drc 1:13.6 For the anti isomer: m.p. 82.5-84.1
°C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.02(d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.57(t, J = 7.4
Hz, 1H), 7.46(t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 4.04(dd, J = 27.9, 9.0 Hz, 1H), 2.03(d,
J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 1.76(d, J = 22.5 Hz, 3H), 0.98(s, 9H); 13C NMR(100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 201.8(d, JCF = 25.1 Hz), 134.8(d, JCF = 4.0 Hz), 133.0, 129.9(d,
JCF = 8.5 Hz), 128.4(d, JCF = 1.5 Hz), 105.4(d, JCF = 194.9 Hz), 80.4(d,
JCF = 21.6 Hz), 36.2, 27.6(d, JCF = 3.5 Hz), 23.8(d, JCF = 24.6 Hz); 19F
NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -166.5(qui, J = 23.6 Hz); IR (neat) ν: 3526(s),
3061(w), 2959(s), 2875(m), 1681(s), 1597(m), 1578(w), 1482(m), 1448(m),
1398(w), 1368(m), 1269(m), 1186(m), 1146(w), 1086(m), 1060(m), 1020(m),
979(m), 794(m), 718(m), 691(m), 659(m) cm-1; MS (ESI) m/z: 261.0 (M+
Na+); HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C14H19FO2 (M+Na+) 261.1261, found
261.1267.
