$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3-3. Enantioselective Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction
of Benzaldehyde with Silyl Enol Ethers of Ketones General Procedures: To
a solution of benzaldehyde 5a (0.10 mmol; 10.6 mg, 1.0 eq) in
toluene/hexanes (1:1(v/v); 0.5 mL) was added chiral Bronsted acid 2e (1.2
mg; 0.001 mmol; 0.01 eq) in toluene/hexanes (1:1(v/v); 0.5 mL). The
mixture was stirred for 30 min at -86 °C. Silyl enol ether of
acetophenone (0.11 mmol; 21.1 mg; 1.1 eq) was added dropwise to the
reaction mixture and the reaction mixture was monitored by TLC. When the
aldehyde was completely consumed, the reaction mixture was quenched with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 and extracted with ether. The resulting aldol
product was dissolved in ether and treated with 1 N HCl to deprotect the
silyl ether. After deprotection was over, the reaction mixture was
extracted with ether. The organic layer was combined, washed with brine,
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated. The residue was purified
by flash column chromatography (EtOAc/hexanes, 1/5) on silica gel.
Enantiomeric ratio (e.r.) was determined by HPLC with a chiral column.
The product (6da) was obtained as colorless oil in 98 % yield and 92:8
er. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ: 2.53 (s, 3H), 3.25-3.35 (m, 2H), 3.57 (d,
J = 3.0 Hz, 1H), 5.31 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 7.22-7.30 (m, 3H), 7.34-7.42
(m, 5H), 7.62 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H).; 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ: 21.7,
50.0, 70.5, 125.9 (2C), 127.8, 128.7, 129.1, 132.0, 132.3, 137.2, 138.8,
143.1, 204.0. Enantiomeric ratio (er) was determined by HPLC with a
Chiralcel OD-H column equipped with an OD-H guard column
(hexanes:2-propanol = 95:5, flow rate = 1.0 mL/min, λ= 254 nm), tr(major,
R) = 18.5 min., tr(minor, S) = 15.9 min.. [α]D 27= +54.2 (c 1.0, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Triflylthiophosphoramide Catalyzed Enantioselective Mukaiyama Aldol
Reaction of Aldehydes with Silyl Enol Ethers of Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cheon, Cheol Hong; Yamamoto, Hisashi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(11), 2476-2479

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME180 STEP1
$RXN



