$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.2. Diastereoselective Mukaiyama aldol
reaction of cyclohexanones with acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)cyclohexyl)acetate (4a) Ethyl
3-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-3-ethyl-2,2-dimethylpentanoate (5b)
According to the synthetic procedure for 4a, this compound was obtained
in 98% yield (312.2 mg, 0.98 mmol) by the reaction of pentan-3-one 2h
(106 μL, 1.0 mmol) with
tert-butyl(1-ethoxy-2-methylpropenyloxy)-dimethylsilane (345.5 mg, 1.5
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) in the presence of Tf2CHCH2CHTf2 1 (5.7 mg, 10
μmol) for 2.5 h at -178 °C. Colorless oil;. IR (neat) ν 2957, 2933, 2857,
1723, 1256, 1111, 1063, 835, 770 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.11
(6H, s), 0.85 (6H, t, J = 7.5 Hz), 0.88 (9H, s), 1.23 (6H, s), 1.25 (3H,
t, J = 7.1 Hz), 1.71-1.88 (4H, m), 4.07 (2H, q, J = 7.1 Hz); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ -10.8, 9.9, 14.4, 19.4, 23.1, 26.6, 28.4, 51.7, 60.6, 82.8,
177.3; MS (ESI-TOF) m/z 339 [M+Na]+; HRMS calcd for C17H36NaO3Si [M+Na]+,
339.2331; found, 339.2347.
