$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Aqueous Mukaiyama
Aldol Reaction. To a mixture of surfactant (0.04 mmol) in water (1 mL)
were added Sc(OTf)3 (0.02 mmol), aldehyde (0.2 mmol), and silyl enol
ether (0.3 mmol). The mixture was stirred at room temperature until the
silyl enol ether disappeared on TLC. Then, the mixture was passed through
a short silica gel pad and extracted with ethyl ether. The combined
organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
The desired aldol adduct. All of the aldol products are known compounds,
and their characterization data were consistent with the literature:
entry 10; 2-[hydroxy-(4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]cyclohexanone (5c): Yield:
97%; syn/anti: 67/33.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, syn:anti 78:22, other surfactants gave lower yields
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Development of Highly Effective Encapsulating Surfactants for Mukaiyama
Aldol Reactions in Water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
