$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Asymmetric Aldol
Reactions Catalyzed by FeII Salt: Mixture of TPS-he-pybox (3c) (47 mg,
0.06 mmol, 12 mol%) and iron(II) chloride (6.5 mg, 0.05 mmol, 10 mol%) in
deoxygenated EtOH/H2O (9/1) 1.5 mL was stirred at 0 °C under Ar until all
the solid was observed to dissolve (15-20 min.). To the resulting
deep-red solution silyl enol ether 5 (230 μL, 1.0 mmol, 2 equivalents)
and appropriate aldehyde (0.5 mmol) were added and resulting solution was
stirred at 0 °C for 5 h under Ar. The reaction was diluted with MTBE and
washed with water and brine. Organic phase was dried, evaporated to
dryness and the residue was purified by silica gel chromatography
(typically, AcOEt/hexane, 1:4).
3-Hydroxy-2-methyl-1,5-diphenyl-pent-4-en-1-one (7i). 1H NMR (200 MHz) δ
(syn): 1.36 (d, 3H, J 7.4 Hz), 3.40 (brs, 1H, OH), 3.64 (dq, 1H, J 3.5,
7.3 Hz), 4.72-4.81 (m, 1H), 6.24 (dd, 1H, J 5.7, 16.0 Hz), 6.71 (dd, 1H,
J 1.4, 16.0 Hz), 7.10-7.70 (m, 8H), 7.80-8.10 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (50 MHz)
δ: 11.9, 45.7, 72.2, 126.4, 127.5, 128.4, 128.8, 128.7, 129.1, 130.9,
133.4, 135.8, 136.6, 205.0. HPLC (Daicel Chiralpak AD-H, hexane/i-PrOH =
9/1, flow rate = 1 mL/min; syn isomer: t1 = 17.8 min, t2 = 21.8 min
(major), anti isomer: t1 = 20.0 min, t2 = 26.9 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama-Aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iron(II) and Zinc(II) Complexes with Designed pybox Ligand for Asymmetric
Aqueous Mukaiyama-Aldol Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
