$DATUM 3.2. Diastereoselective Mukaiyama aldol reaction of cyclohexanones with
acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)cyclohexyl)acetate (4a) To a solution of
cyclohexanone 2a (103.5 μL, 1.0 mmol) and Tf2CHCH2CHTf2 1 (0.29 mg, 0.5
μmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL), a solution of
tert-butyl(1-ethoxyvinyloxy)dimethylsilane (303.5 mg, 1.5 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(1.0 mL) was added at -178 °C over 90 min via syringe pump. After being
stirred at the same temperature for additional 1 h, the reaction mixture
was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (20 mL), and
extracted with EtOAc (20 mL x 3). The combined organic layer was dried
over anhydrous MgSO4 and evaporated. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc = 80 : 1) to give aldol
product 4a in 98% yield (293.3 mg, 0.98 mmol). Colorless oil;. IR (neat)
ν 2929, 2850, 1739, 1254, 1061, 836, 773 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
0.07 (6H, s), 0.84 (9H, s), 1.23 (3H, t, J = 7.1 Hz), 1.29-1.43 (4H, m),
1.49-1.59 (2H, m), 1.59-1.69 (2H, m), 1.69-1.80 (2H, m), 2.48 (2H, s),
4.08 (2H, q, J = 7.1 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ -12.0, 14.2, 18.2,
22.8, 25.5, 25.8, 38.4, 46.3, 60.0, 74.5, 171.0; MS (ESI-TOF) m/z 323
[M+Na]+; HRMS calcd for C16H32NaO3Si [M+Na]+, 323.2018; found, 323.1991.
Anal. Calcd for C16H32O3Si: C, 63.95; H, 10.73. Found: C, 63.80; H,
10.63.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Carbon Acid Induced Mukaiyama Aldol Type Reaction of Sterically Hindered
Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
