$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for catalytic Mukaiyama
aldol reactions Toluene (1.5 mL) was added to a condensed phase of 2a,
prepared as mentioned above from Et3SiH (1.6 μL, 10 μmol) and
Ph3CB(C6F5)4 (4.6 mg, 5.0 μmol). The mixture was cooled to -78 °C
followed by addition of 3-pentanone (53 μL, 0.50 mmol) and
1-phenyl-1-trimethylsiloxyethane (110 μL, 0.55 mmol) successively. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C. The reaction was then
quenched by slow addition of 1 M aq. HCl / THF (1 : 1, 0.5 mL). The
reaction mixture was warmed to room temperature and neutralized by
saturated aq. NaHCO3 (0.5 mL). The aqueous phase was extracted three
times with CH2Cl2. The combined organic phase was dried over MgSO4 and
solvent was removed in vacuo. Purification by column chromatography on
silica gel (10% EtOAc / Hexane) afforded the addition product 5ba in 96%
yield. 1,3-Diphenyl-3-hydroxy-1-butanone (5aa): 5
3-Ethyl-3-hydroxy-1-phenyl-1-pentanone (5ba), yield 97% 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
0.91 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 6H), 1.56-1.69 (m, 4H), 3.11 (s, 2H), 4.06 (s, 1H),
7.46-7.51 (m, 2H), 7.58-7.63 (m, 1H), 7.95-7.98 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Strong Counteranion Effects on the Catalytic Activity of Cationic Silicon
Lewis Acids in Mukaiyama Aldol and Diels-Alder Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hara, Kenji; Akiyama, Ryuto; Sawamura, Masaya
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(25), 5621-5623

