$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-3. Enantioselective Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction of Benzaldehyde with Silyl
Enol Ethers of Ketones General Procedures: To a solution of benzaldehyde
5a (0.10 mmol; 10.6 mg, 1.0 eq) in toluene/hexanes (1:1(v/v); 0.5 mL) was
added chiral Bronsted acid 2e (1.2 mg; 0.001 mmol; 0.01 eq) in
toluene/hexanes (1:1(v/v); 0.5 mL). The mixture was stirred for 30 min at
-86 °C. Silyl enol ether of acetophenone (0.11 mmol; 21.1 mg; 1.1 eq) was
added dropwise to the reaction mixture and the reaction mixture was
monitored by TLC. When the aldehyde was completely consumed, the reaction
mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 and extracted with
ether. The resulting aldol product was dissolved in ether and treated
with 1 N HCl to deprotect the silyl ether. After deprotection was over,
the reaction mixture was extracted with ether. The organic layer was
combined, washed with brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography
(EtOAc/hexanes, 1/5) on silica gel. Enantiomeric ratio (e.r.) was
determined by HPLC with a chiral column. The product (6ba)11 was obtained
as a white solid in 97 % yield and 92:8 er. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ:
3.29-3.34 (m, 2H), 3.76 (br, 1H), 3.89 (s, 3H), 5.31-5.34 (dd, J = 8.5,
3.0 Hz, 1H), 6.93 (dt, J = 9.5 Hz, 2.5 Hz, 2H), 7.30 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
7.38 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 7.43 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.92 (dt, J = 9.5,
2.5 Hz, 2H).; 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ: 47.1, 55.7, 70.3, 114.0, 125.9,
127.8, 128.7, 129.8, 130.6, 143.2, 164.1, 198.9. Enantiomeric ratio (er)
was determined by HPLC with a Chiralcel IB column equipped with an IB
guard column (hexanes:2-propanol = 95:5, flow rate = 1.0 mL/min, λ= 254
nm), tr(major) = 24.8 min., tr(minor) = 28.0 min.. [α]D 27= +39.7 (c 1.0,
CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mukaiyama aldol reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Triflylthiophosphoramide Catalyzed Enantioselective Mukaiyama Aldol
Reaction of Aldehydes with Silyl Enol Ethers of Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cheon, Cheol Hong; Yamamoto, Hisashi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(11), 2476-2479

