$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Mukaiyama Aldol
Reaction of α-OTMP-Aldehyde and Silyl ketene Acetals. An oven-dried vial
was flushed with dry N2, charged with TiCl2(OiPr)2 (2.0 equiv.) and
CH2Cl2 (0.2 M), and cooled to -20 °C.
(R)-3-(benzyloxy)-2-(2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidin-1-yloxy)propanal (90%
ee, 1.0 equiv.) and the silyl ketene acetal (2.0 equiv.) were weighed
into an Eppendorf tube, dissolved in a minimum amount of CH2Cl2, and
added to the solution of TiCl2(OiPr)2 via a microliter syringe. The
mixture was stirred for 16 hours at -20 °C, then quenched by the addition
of sat. aq. NH4Cl (2 mL) and poured over H2O (10 mL). The aqueous layer
was extracted with Et2O (3 x 5 mL) and the combined organic layers were
dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under vacuum. The crude
product was purified by flash chromatography.
Isopropy1-((1S,2R)-3-(benzyloxy)-1-hydroxy-2-((2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidin-1-yl)oxy)propyl)cyclopentanecarboxylate
(15a). The compound was synthesized following the general procedure using
TiCl2(OiPr)2 (190 mg, 800 μmol, 2.0 equiv.),
(R)-3-(benzyloxy)-2-(2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidin-1- yloxy)propanal (90%
ee, 128 mg, 400 μmol, 1.0 equiv.),
(cyclopentylidene(isopropoxy)methoxy)trimethylsilane (183 mg, 800 μmol,
2.0 equiv.) and CH2Cl2 (2 mL). The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography using 9:1 hexanes:Et2O to yield the title compound (183
mg, 96% yield, >20:1) as a colorless oil. Due to the similar structural
features and the consistent NMR-data of the title compound to
(3S,4R)-isopropyl 5-(benzyloxy)-3-hydroxy-2,2-
dimethy4-((2,2,6,6-tetramethylpiperidin-1-yl)oxy)pentanoate (see above)
the configuration of the title compound was assigned as ribo/arabino. IR
(thin film): 3489, 2967, 2934, 2871, 1723, 1494, 1467, 1454, 1375, 1360,
1259, 1237, 1206, 1181, 1130, 1107, 1075, 1047, 991, 956, 910, 878, 824,
787, 735, 698 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.42-7.26 (m, 5H, ArH),
4.97 (sept, 1H, J = 6.2 Hz, CH(CH3)2), 4.56 (d, 1H, J = 11.6 Hz, CHaPh),
4.52 (d, 1H, J = 11.6 Hz, CHbPh), 4.23 (dd, 1H, J = 5.7, 5.6 Hz, CHOH),
4.15-4.08 (m, 1H, CHOTMP), 3.95-3.88 (m, 2H, CH2OBn), 3.86 (d, 1H, J =
6.3 Hz, OH), 2.29-0.99 (m, 26H, OTMP, (CH2)4), 1.24 (d, 3H, J = 6.3 Hz,
CH(CH3)a), 1.22 (d, 3H, J = 6.3 Hz, CH(CH3)b); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 176.1 (CO2 iPr), 137.7, 128.4, 127.8, 127.8 (ArC), 81.0 (CHOTMP), 76.9
(CHOH), 73.5 (CH2Ph), 70.7 (CH2OBn), 67.7 (CH(CH3)2), 60.6, 59.6
((CH3)2CNC(CH3)2), 57.5 (CCO2 iPr), 40.7, 40.4 (CCH2CH2CH2C), 35.3
(CH2CH2CCH2CH2), 34.3, 33.3 ((CH3)aCNC(CH3)a), 30.6 (CH2CH2CCH2CH2),
25.7, 25.4 (CH2CH2CCH2CH2), 21.6, 21.6 (CH(CH3)2), 20.8, 20.8
((CH3)bCNC(CH3)b), 17.2 (CCH2CH2CH2C); HRMS (ESI-TOF) calculated for
C28H45NO5 [M+H]+ m/z 476.3371, found 476.3368; αD 21 = -35.2 (c = 1.00,
CHCl3).
