$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.2. Diastereoselective Mukaiyama aldol
reaction of cyclohexanones with acyclic ketene acetals Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)cyclohexyl)acetate (4a) Ethyl
(1-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2,2-dimethylcyclohexyl)acetate (4e)
According to the synthetic procedure for 4a, this compound was obtained
in 96% yield (315.2 mg, 0.96 mmol) by the reaction of
2,2-dimethylcyclohexanone 2d (138 μL, 1.0 mmol) with
tert-butyl(1-ethoxyvinyloxy)-dimethylsilane (303.0 mg, 1.5 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) in the presence of Tf2CHCH2CHTf2 1 (2.9 mg, 5.0 μmol) for
3 h at -178 °C. Colorless oil;. IR (neat) ν 3017, 2833, 1737, 1094, 835,
772 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.05 (3H, s), 0.10 (3H, s), 0.89 (9H,
s), 0.90 (3H, s), 0.96 (3H, s), 1.13-1.22 (1H, m), 1.24 (3H, t, J = 7.1
Hz), 1.38-1.76 (6H, m), 2.00-2.09 (1H, m), 2.50 (1H, d, J = 13.5 Hz),
2.69 (1H, d, J = 13.5 Hz), 3.97-4.19 (2H, m); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
-11.8 and -11.7, 14.1, 18.9, 21.3, 23.0, 24.0 and 24.5, 26.2, 32.1, 39.7,
41.7, 60.0, 79.6, 171.7; MS (ESI-TOF) m/z 351 [M+Na] +; HRMS calcd for
C18H36NaO3Si [M+Na]+, 351.2331; found, 351.2317. Anal. Calcd for
C18H36O3Si: C, 65.80; H, 11.04. Found: C, 65.54; H, 10.90.
