$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 9. A general procedure for 5b·L2-catalyzed Mannich-type reactions:
Freshly distilled THF (4 mL) was injected at room temperature under
nitrogen into pyrex Schrenk tube containing sodium phenoxide (5b) (11.6
mg, 0.10 mmol) and L (95.6 mg, 0.20 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10
min at that temperature, and then this colorless solution was cooled to
–78 °C and stirred for 5 min at that temperature. Silyl enolate (2.4
mmol), and then imine (2 mmol) were added. The pale yellow-orange
solution was stirred at –40 °C for 18 h by monitoring with TLC, and the
reaction mixture was diluted with sat. NaHCO3 aqueous solution (10 mL).
The mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate (15 mL × 2), and the
combined organic layer was washed by brine (10 mL), dried over MgSO4 and
evaporated under reduced pressure to give the Mannich-type product which
was purified by flash neutral silica gel column chromatography
(hexane/AcOEt = 5/1–1/1). phenyl
3-(tert-butoxycarbonylamino)-2,2-dimethyl-3-phenylpropanoate (7f). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.26 (s, 3H), 1.39 (s, 9H), 1.44 (s, 3H), 4.92 (d, J =
9.6 Hz, 1H), 5.94 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1H), 6.98 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
7.20-7.42 (m, 10H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 22.1, 24.5, 28.3, 47.1,
61.2, 79.5, 121.5, 125.9, 127.6, 128.0, 128.1, 129.4, 139.1, 150.5,
155.2, 175.2. IR(KBr) 3364, 2979, 1741, 1700, 1519, 1366, 1242, 1192,
1168, 1114 cm-1. HRMS(FAB+) calcd for C22H28NO4 [M+H]+ 370.2018, found
370.2017.
