$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure for the Catalytic Asymmetric Vinylogous
Mukaiyama Aldol Addition: Preparation of
(E)-(R)-5-hydroxy-2-methyl-7-phenyl-hept- 2-enethioic acid S-tert-butyl
ester SI4. To a 15 mL round-bottom flask with 4Å molecular sieves (0.298
g, 400 mg/mmol aldehyde) and (S)-BINOL (43.0 mg, 149 μmol, 0.20 eq) at
room temperature were added Et2O (2.0 mL, 0.35 M) and Ti(OiPr)4 (1.00 M
in CH2Cl2, 75 μL, 75 μmol, 0.10 eq). The red-brown mixture was heated to
40 °C. The mixture was cooled to room temperature after 1 h, and
hydrocinnamaldehyde (98 μL, 0.75 mmol, 1.0 eq) was added. The mixture was
stirred for 20 min at room temperature, trimethyl borate (42 μL, 0.37
mmol, 0.50 eq) was added and the mixture cooled to -78 °C. Diene SI3 (397
μL, 1.49 mmol, 2.00 eq) was added, the mixture stirred for 30 min at -78
°C and then warmed to room temperature. After 4 d a saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 solution (2 mL) was added, the mixture stirred for 30 min, diluted
with CH2Cl2 (20 mL) and filtered through a plug of Celite®. The organic
phase washed with water (10 and 15 mL) and brine (5 mL), dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, concentrated under reduced pressure, and purified by
flash chromatography on a 2.5 × 18 cm silica gel column eluting with a
solvent mixture of 5% acetone/hexanes (900 mL). The eluant was collected
in 30 mL portions and the product containing fractions (11 to 24) were
combined and concentrated to give alcohol SI4 (217 mg, 708 mmol, 95%
yield) as a clear colorless liquid. The ratio of enantiomers was
determined to be er = 7 : 93 (with BF3•EtO2 as Lewis-acid er = 50 : 50)
by HPLC analysis using a Daicel Chiralcel OD-H silica column, eluting
with a mobile phase of 15% 2-propanol/hexanes and a flow rate of 0.5
mL/min, which gave the retention times for the minor (S) and major (R)
enantiomers of 12.6 and 14.6 min, respectively, detecting with a Rainin
Dynamax Refractive Index Detector Model RI-1: Rf 0.33 (25%
EtOAc/hexanes); [α]D 20 +6.3 (c = 0.960, CHCl3, er = 96 : 4); 500 MHz 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.32 – 7.27 (m, 2H), 7.22 – 7.29 (m, 3H), 6.72 (ddq, J =
7.3, 7.3, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 3.79 (dddd, J = 12.6, 5.6, 5.6, 5.4 Hz, 1H), 2.83
(ddd, J = 14.0, 7.3, 6.9 Hz, 1H), 2.71 (ddd, J = 14.6, 7.1, 6.4 Hz, 1H),
2.40 – 2.37 (m, 2H), 1.86 (s, 3H), 1.85 – 1.81 (m, 2H), 1.50 (s, 9H),
C5OH not observed; 125 MHz 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 195.0, 141.9, 139.3, 135.2,
128.7 (2), 128.6 (2), 126.2, 70.6, 47.7, 38.9, 37.0, 32.2, 30.1 (3),
12.9; 125 MHz DEPT (CDCl3) δ CH3: 30.1 (3), 12.9. CH2: 38.9, 37.1, 32.3.
CH: 135.3, 128.7 (2), 128.7 (2), 126.2, 70.6. C: 195.0, 141.9, 139.3,
47.7; IR (neat) 3425 (bs), 3063, 3027, 2999, 2962, 2923, 2863, 1650,
1496, 1477, 1455, 1390, 1363, 1162, 1051,1030, 987, 934, 897, 747, 700,
662 cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C18H26O2S: C, 70.54; H, 8.55. Found: C, 70.74;
H, 8.63.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 4A mol. sieves used, optimization study, optimized on
borate loading and reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Catalytic Asymmetric Vinylogous Mukaiyama Aldol Reaction
